# Copy to .env.local and change what you need. Everything here has a working
# default, so MySenam runs with none of it set — but two of them should never
# reach production untouched.

# The country this install serves: MY (default) or SG. Currency, phone
# numbers, time zone, languages, map and the default payment gateway follow it.
# MYSENAM_COUNTRY=MY

# What the site calls itself. A venue business's own copy uses its own name.
# SITE_NAME=MySenam

# The shared marketplace: venues apply to join and stored credit is per venue.
# Leave unset for one business's own copy.
# MYSENAM_MARKETPLACE=on
# MYSENAM_CREDIT_SCOPE=venue
#
# What venues pay to be listed, invoiced on the first of each month, and how
# many months a newly approved venue gets free.
# MYSENAM_VENUE_FEE=99
# MYSENAM_FREE_MONTHS=0
#
# The operator's own SST or GST, once registered: added to venues' invoices.
# Both the rate and the number, or no tax. MYSENAM_TAX_NAME overrides SST/GST.
# MYSENAM_TAX_RATE=8
# MYSENAM_TAX_REG_NO=W10-0000-00000000
#
# Payment gateways venues may connect (comma-separated), and the one the
# platform's own account is at. Billplz is the only one so far.
# MYSENAM_PAYMENT_PROVIDERS=billplz
# MYSENAM_PAYMENT_PROVIDER=billplz
#
# The platform's own Billplz account, which venues pay their invoices into.
# Not a venue's: venues enter their own under Venues & staff → Online payment.
# BILLPLZ_API_KEY=
# BILLPLZ_COLLECTION_ID=
# BILLPLZ_X_SIGNATURE_KEY=
# BILLPLZ_SANDBOX=on

# Who runs the site, shown in the terms at /terms.
# OPERATOR_NAME=
# OPERATOR_REG_NO=
# OPERATOR_ADDRESS=
# OPERATOR_EMAIL=

# The first operator account, created on a fresh database.
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@mysenam.my
# CHANGE THIS. The default is printed in the README, so leaving it is the same
# as having no password at all.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=mysenam-admin

# The database. In production, a Postgres server (16 or later):
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://mysenam:password@127.0.0.1:5432/mysenam
# Unset, it is PGlite — Postgres inside the app — in data/pglite, which is fine
# for development and needs no server, but costs the app about a gigabyte of
# memory. DATABASE_URL=pglite:/some/folder puts that somewhere else.
# DATABASE_POOL_SIZE=10
#
# The app's own folder: backups, and secret.key when MYSENAM_SECRET is unset.
# Put it on a disk that survives a redeploy.
# MYSENAM_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/mysenam

# Where backups are written (default: backups/ in the data folder), and how
# many are kept. On a Postgres server they are taken with pg_dump, which must
# be installed on the machine the app runs on (apt install postgresql-client).
# MYSENAM_BACKUP_DIR=/var/backups/mysenam
# MYSENAM_BACKUP_KEEP=14
# The server takes one every night at this hour, Malaysia time. Set
# MYSENAM_SCHEDULER=off to run `npm run backup` from your own cron instead.
# MYSENAM_BACKUP_HOUR=3
# MYSENAM_SCHEDULER=off
#
# And copies each one off the machine, to any S3-compatible storage
# (Cloudflare R2, Backblaze B2, Amazon S3). Expire old copies with a lifecycle
# rule on the bucket, and give this key permission to write only.
# OFFSITE_S3_ENDPOINT=https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# OFFSITE_S3_BUCKET=venue-backups
# OFFSITE_S3_REGION=auto
# OFFSITE_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# OFFSITE_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# OFFSITE_S3_PREFIX=mysenam/

# Sending messages to customers.
#
# Confirmations, cancellations and waitlist offers are always written down —
# the admin panel shows them under Venues — but nothing leaves the machine
# until this says how. Unset, they queue up and the dashboard says so.
#
#   log   write each message to the server log and mark it sent. For
#         development, and for seeing what a customer would actually receive.
#
# Leave MYSENAM_SEND unset to send for real through whichever of these is set.
# MYSENAM_SEND=log
#
# WhatsApp Cloud API. The five templates in the README must be approved first.
# WHATSAPP_TOKEN=
# WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
# WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_PREFIX=mysenam
# WHATSAPP_COUNTRY_CODE=60
#
# Email, through any SMTP account.
# SMTP_URL=smtp://user:password@smtp.example.com:587
# MAIL_FROM=Arena Bookings <bookings@example.com>

# Where this install is reachable, for the links inside those messages.
# Without it they point at localhost, which is no use to a customer.
# MYSENAM_URL=https://book.yourvenue.my

# Encrypts the payment keys venues enter under Online payment. Unset, a key is
# generated into secret.key in the data folder (never in the database, so backups
# carry the locked keys without what unlocks them). Set it to keep payment keys
# working when the database is restored onto another machine.
# MYSENAM_SECRET=
